# Audits App

TypeScript migration completed with unified structure matching `application-list` (index/bootstrap/ui + pages/components). Routes are lazily code-split and heavy chart pages are loaded on demand. All pages and core components are strongly typed and use router-provided lifecycle/context and signals/effect.

**NEW: Patient Management with Form Entries** - Now integrated with Forms Service and Patient Service microservices for full CRUD operations and real-time form entry management using the `asc-schema-form` web component.

## Structure

- src/index.ts: entry; imports CSS and calls bootstrap()
- src/bootstrap.ts: initializes chrome, branding, and router
- src/ui.ts: signals + UI helpers (toast, setActiveBranding, initChrome)
- src/router-config.ts: central typed router with dynamic imports for heavy pages
- src/pages/: route components (TypeScript)
  - dashboards.ts, kpis.ts, charts.ts, benchmarks.ts, patients.ts, support.ts, copd-chart.ts, test.ts
- src/components/: reusable UI building blocks (TypeScript)
  - patient/: PatientSearchCommand.ts, PatientTableReactive.ts, PatientTableUsage.ts, AdvancedSearchContent.ts
  - search/: CriterionRow.ts, SearchDropdown.ts
  - stats/: StatsCards.ts
- src/pages/data/: typed data helpers (TypeScript)

Notes:

- Charts and COPD pages align with Highcharts v12 options (zooming, panning.enabled, dash styles) and use modular series types. Exporting can be lazy-loaded if needed.
- Router uses extensionless imports; Rspack resolves `.ts` first. Components/pages accept `ComponentDataContext<T>` and `ComponentLifecycleManager` from `@asc/router`.

## Develop

- Start dev server:

```pwsh
bun run --cwd apps/audits dev
```

- Build:

```pwsh
bun run --cwd apps/audits build
```

- Preview prod build:

```pwsh
bun run --cwd apps/audits preview
```

## Highlights

- Code-splitting for heavy routes (charts and children) to keep main entry small
- Shared UI helpers (toast, branding) and signals
- Strongly typed router lifecycle/context wiring for all pages
- Patients page demonstrates Command search + reactive table with typed signals and callbacks

## Next steps (optional)

- Add small unit tests for router config and UI helpers
- Add lazy loading of Highcharts exporting on charts (currently enabled on COPD chart)

# Rspack project

## Setup

Install the dependencies:

```pwsh
bun install
```

## Get started

Start the dev server:

```pwsh
bun run dev
```

Build the app for production:

```pwsh
bun run build
```
